    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d614-a1">

                <pb facs="0789" n="695" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg695"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 89.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Messrs. Atkins &amp; Co. to
                        Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Boston, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: We hand you herewith copy of a
                    circular letter sent to our place (Soledad) by the secretary of the treasury of
                    the so-called Cuban Republic, which communication we submit for your
                    information.</p>
                <p>Our general manager declined to make the payment, and notified the Spanish
                    authorities of the matter.</p>
                <pb facs="0790" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>
                <p>The letter does not state where the treasury of the Republic is located, and the
                    payment of the tax only exempts the buildings and machinery from destruction
                    providing that no attempt is made to operate the mills.</p>
                <p>Yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Atkins</hi> &amp; Co.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
